  "about_content": "<h2><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"2\" style=\"vertical-align:middle;margin-right:8px\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"4\"/></svg>Why we built YonoappDex</h2>\n<p>Type \"Yono games\" into a search engine and you get a mess. You see copied websites, fake download buttons, modded APK files with the same name from different makers, and blogs that claim every game is the best just to get your click.</p>\n<p>Because of that clutter, ordinary players end up installing apps they know nothing about from sources they cannot verify. We built YonoappDex to fix that. We wanted one clean, straightforward place where a game is explained in plain words and its real maker is easy to check before anyone hits install.</p>\n\n<h2><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"2\" style=\"vertical-align:middle;margin-right:8px\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20\"/><path d=\"M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z\"/></svg>What we do</h2>\n<p>YonoappDex is a free information directory. Our motto is simple: <strong>know the game before you download it</strong>. We sort free Yono games into clear categories—<a href=\"/card-games\">card</a>, <a href=\"/casual-games\">casual</a>, <a href=\"/board-games\">board</a>, <a href=\"/arcade-games\">arcade</a>, and <a href=\"/casino-style-games\">free casino-style</a>—and write a dedicated profile for each title.</p>\n\n<h3>What goes into a game profile</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Plain-English rules:</strong> What kind of game it is and how a round actually plays.</li>\n  <li><strong>Ads and purchases:</strong> How the free game makes money, including ad frequency and in-app item sales.</li>\n  <li><strong>Phone permissions:</strong> What access the app asks for on your device, flagging anything unusual like contacts or SMS access.</li>\n  <li><strong>Chat and online rooms:</strong> Whether the game lets players talk to strangers, so parents can check before handing over a phone.</li>\n  <li><strong>Maker and review date:</strong> Who built the game, the version we looked at, and the exact date we last checked the facts.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"2\" style=\"vertical-align:middle;margin-right:8px\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M8 12l3 3 5-6\"/></svg>How we review and label games</h2>\n<p>We write every profile from public records: official listings on <a href=\"https://play.google.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Google Play</a> and the <a href=\"https://www.apple.com/in/app-store/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apple App Store</a>, verified developer websites, and published game rules. We do not inspect private source code, decompile APK files, or play-test every level of every game.</p>\n\n<h3>What our labels mean</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Official Source Confirmed (Green Tick):</strong> We checked the developer's identity, confirmed the game is free to play without real-money cash-outs, and matched our link to the official store page or developer website. Only these pages get a download link.</li>\n  <li><strong>Source Not Verified:</strong> We could not confirm where the game comes from. We publish the information so you know what it is, but we leave the download link out.</li>\n  <li><strong>Under Review:</strong> We are still checking the details, or we have temporarily removed the link after a user report.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You can read our full step-by-step process on <a href=\"/how-we-review-games\">How We Review Games</a>.</p>\n\n<h2><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"2\" style=\"vertical-align:middle;margin-right:8px\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 3l8 3v6c0 4.5-3.2 8.3-8 9-4.8-.7-8-4.5-8-9V6z\"/></svg>Editorial independence</h2>\n<p>We do not sell rankings, green ticks, or favourable reviews. A developer cannot pay us to list a game, hide a permission warning, or push their app to the top of a category. Games earn a link solely by being free to play and having an official source we can confirm.</p>\n<p>If a developer or rights owner asks us to change something on a profile, we update it only when the public facts support the change.</p>\n\n<h2><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2\" style=\"vertical-align:middle;margin-right:8px\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M12 8h.01M11 12h1v5h1\"/></svg>What we are not</h2>\n<p>To keep things completely clear for visitors, developers, and regulators:</p>\n\n<h3>No connection with SBI or YONO banking</h3>\n<p>YonoappDex is an independent game directory. We have no connection, affiliation, or partnership with <a href=\"https://sbi.co.in/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">State Bank of India (SBI)</a>, the official YONO SBI banking application, or any bank or financial service. We use the word \"Yono\" only in its common search sense to describe a category of mobile games, as explained in our <a href=\"/legal-notice\">Legal Notice</a>.</p>\n\n<h3>Not an APK host or game studio</h3>\n<p>We do not make games, run game servers, or handle player accounts. We also do not host, store, or share APK files or installation packages on our servers. When a link is shown, it takes you straight to the official store or developer site under our <a href=\"/download-policy\">Download Policy</a>.</p>\n\n<h3>No real-money gambling</h3>\n<p>We do not list real-money games. If a game offers cash deposits, betting, or coins that can be withdrawn or swapped for money or vouchers, it is kept off this site.</p>\n\n<h2><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1a73e8\" stroke-width=\"2\" style=\"vertical-align:middle;margin-right:8px\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"5\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M3 7l9 6 9-6\"/></svg>How we handle reports and get in touch</h2>\n<p>Developers update apps all the time without telling us. If you spot a broken link, outdated information, or a listed game that has added real-money features, click the <strong>Report this game</strong> button on the game page. No account is needed. For safety and real-money reports, we aim to take the link down within 24 hours and check the details afterwards under our <a href=\"/report-and-removal-policy\">Report and Removal Policy</a>.</p>\n\n<h3>Contact and Grievance Officer</h3>\n<p>We operate in line with the <a href=\"https://www.indiacode.nic.in/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Information Technology Act, 2000</a> and the <a href=\"https://www.meity.gov.in/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023</a>. For general questions, game requests, corrections, or formal legal notices, write to us:</p>\n<p><strong>Govardhan Das</strong>, Grievance Officer, YonoappDex<br>\n<a href=\"mailto:support@yonoappdex.com\">support@yonoappdex.com</a></p>\n<p><em>Last updated: 3 November 2026</em></p>\n",
  "about_meta_description": "Learn why we built YonoappDex, how we review free Yono games using public sources, what our green tick means, and why we stay completely independent.",
